  "tagline": "Gremlin graph layer on the Aerospike database for billion-edge graphs with predictable latency.",
  "description": "Aerospike Graph is a property-graph service from Aerospike that implements Apache TinkerPop/Gremlin as a stateless query tier on top of the Aerospike key-value database, which handles storage, sharding and replication. Because compute and storage scale separately and Aerospike is built for SSD-backed low-latency access, it targets identity graphs, ad-tech and fraud workloads with billions of vertices and strict latency budgets. It suits teams already running Aerospike or committed to Gremlin, but it brings a commercial license and no Cypher or GQL support.",
